  "interpretation": {
    "event_order_and_identity": "All 9,962 paired event rows retain identical order, event kind, node/peer and application/hop identity. Twenty release snapshots retain differing resend/hold intermediate states; not strict semantic table equality.",
    "feedback_kind": "Seven per case are MATLAB DACK vs native ACK, all carrying identical ACK and DACK bitmaps; no added feedback envelope or changed custody outcome. Native HOP constructs cumulative DACK with IsAck=true and IsDack=true. Native MAC DoTx chooses type by IsAck first, rewriting to ACK; MATLAB retains frame.Kind=DACK. Native csr-net-device.h SHA112f9ac73e2ced44a40d6fcc3dc0a8d2cf19996f4f1d52adb0b9a5fbfe103dfb and csr-hop-layer.h SHA0a826930bab43db429a2a3bd905672b370774274f7de826abf180f002156f10b both match T13 reference native_source_hashes. Exact kind differences remain explicit.",
    "release_state": "MATLAB complete moves resend to DackHolds and removes resend before releaseNsdp. Native HandleDackFrame calls NotifyNsdpFromEntry before creating DackEntry and erasing resend. Thus each of20 DACK custody callbacks has -1 resend/+1 hold in MATLAB; total HOP pending and NWK custody agree.",
    "startup_offset": "Every nonzero event time delta and every draw/TX/arrival/terminal delta in nanosecond mode is exactly -28ns. Unshifted events have zero delta. No accumulating drift occurs within this64s fixture. This reproduces the previously documented native startup phase; T15 deliberately does not alter startup.",
    "boundary_distance": "All393 outage transport rows recompute their nearest boundary distance exactly from actual TX time. Differences are +/-28ns from startup offset; loss decisions/reasons and group identity match.",
    "scope": "Fixed routes, controlled loss, prescribed draws, portable runtime; no full-network parity."
  }
